Z||000006||FieroGTguy||05-12-2001||03:19 PM||||The great thing about where your kit is headed is that it is partable.  In other words, a person can upgrade the kit a part at a time.  Be sure to sell each bumper kit, rocker scoop kit, and other parts of the kit individually.  Then cut a better deal on the complete kit.  I think you will find much more success that way.  (not to mention the lost customers that would buy one part, but wouldn't want to buy the kit)  You could even price individual pieces (like each corner to the front bumper) for those who get into frequent fender benders.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Also, since you are rating multiple manufacturers...  Some could make certain pieces cheaper than others.  They may try to steepen the price if they new that they were your sole provider of the entire kit.  Plus, you could rate their quality when the pieces come in from the different places.  If one doesn't meet your specifications, give the business to the ones you do like.  (and be sure to let them know that the higher quality parts you see, the more business and parts you will allow them to make)  <P>Just a thought.<P>Greg||||reg||1
